{"repositoryId":1239928097,"availability":"available","full":"falcon4ever/kanama","name":"kanama","description":"Kanama brings Kotlin to Godot through a GDExtension runtime powered by the JVM and the Foreign Function & Memory API.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Kotlin","stars":17,"forks":2,"created":"2026-05-15T15:33:20Z","updated":"2026-10-15T13:49:47Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://falcon4ever.github.io/kanama/","topics":[],"demo":"https://falcon4ever.github.io/kanama/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:21.101Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:21.101Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:21.101Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T15:01:21.101Z","stars":17,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Kotlin for Godot through a GDExtension runtime powered by the JVM and the Foreign Function & Memory API.","Kanama lets Kotlin scripts attach to Godot nodes through a GDExtension runtime. In the Godot editor, Kanama .kt files appear as script resources and can be attached directly to nodes like .gd scripts. Kanama aims to preserve the Godot workflow while giving game code access to Kotlin, Gradle, coroutines, and the JVM ecosystem."],"features":["Kotlin scripts attach to Godot nodes like GDScript","No engine fork, no engine module, no JNI glue in game code","Desktop runtime powered by the JDK Foreign Function & Memory API","Android runtime through Godot's Android plugin AAR flow (ART + PanamaPort)","iOS runtime through a Kotlin/Native .xcframework, no on-device JVM"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/falcon4ever/kanama/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"bfef4b98cb8b71c1aad30bba04f09f7f594625972f3399fe8488e7c9eb65aa2d","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:21.360Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:21.360Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Kotlin for Godot through a GDExtension runtime powered by the JVM and the Foreign Function & Memory API.","source